# A `.env` that defines the same name twice.
#
# `resolve.ParseDotEnv` — the one reader of this format — takes the LAST, because
# each line overwrites the map entry before it, and that is what `docker compose`
# does too. The refusal that says "already set to X at .env:N" therefore has to
# name the last line as well: pointing the reader at line 13 while quoting the
# value from line 14 sends them to edit the line that is not in effect.
#
# The commented-out third line is the case people actually create — the old value
# commented out BELOW the new one. It needs no special handling, because the `#`
# stays attached to the key and so never matches the name; it is here so that is
# asserted rather than assumed.
DUPLICATE=first
DUPLICATE=second
# DUPLICATE=commented-out
